ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"12c7cf9be80223d8b23d3f127089385c4ca158cff78d0fbeeffe4122124a0e78","event_uuid":"fd3696e6-e759-4bdf-b8e1-341a1e403c99","position":{"commit_sha":"4316da7e2f1b9263973a2952ffaf96bdcafc7ab3","position":"1787182806113022001-fd3696e6-e759-4bdf-b8e1-341a1e403c99"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-235_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"eff19c3d-071a-47b5-bae6-8b48a3343a8c","comments":[],"created_at":1787175838286395001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py` is **799 LOC** against the locked\n800-LOC cap (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so the next agent to touch it — even to add a comment\n— fails the CI module-size gate. Gerrit 1916 failed exactly that way on a sibling file.\n\n## Approach\nSplit along the seam the module's own **call graph and import graph already draw**: two disjoint\nfunction clusters that share no module-level import except `logging`.\n\n**Cluster A — event-file materialisation (MOVES).** `_RECONCILER_MARKER_APPLIER`, the four\n`_inbound_create_*` phase helpers (`:153-339`) and the four `_inbound_update_write_edit_event` /\n`_write_status_event` / `_apply_labels` / `_apply_comments` helpers (`:347-545`) — every one\nterminates in `inbound_translate._write_event_file`.\n\n**Cluster B — rebar-facade mutation (STAYS).** `_identity_provider_for` /\n`_ensure_inbound_assignee_identity` (`:54-145`) and the closed link sub-graph\n`_inbound_update_apply_links` → `_open_impossible_link_store` / `_open_peer_confirmation_store` /\n`_skip_impossible_link` / `_note_impossible_link` / `_inbound_unlink_one` (`:548-799`). These write\nthrough the `rebar` facade (`ensure_identity_for`, `link`, `unlink`) and the two sidecar stores,\nare best-effort/fail-open with `logger` reporting, and write NO event files.\n\nCluster B keeps EXACTLY ONE name from the module-level block: `_extract_name`, used at\n`apply_inbound_records.py:123` (`display_name = _extract_name(assignee) or ...`) inside\n`_ensure_inbound_assignee_identity`. So its retained module-level imports are `logging` plus\n`from rebar_reconciler.inbound_translate import _extract_name`; every OTHER name in the block\n(`sys`, `TYPE_CHECKING`/`Any`, `_backend.TicketTransport`, `projects_store`,\n`batch_dispatch._call_with_retry`, the other 12 `inbound_translate` names at `:31-44`) has cluster A\nas its only consumer and moves with it. Cluster B's remaining dependencies are already\nfunction-local imports.\n\nCluster A moves verbatim to a new sibling `apply_inbound_events.py`. Cluster B keeps the existing\nfile — and therefore its `logger` and module identity — because two tests bind to that module\nOBJECT and would silently stop testing anything if it moved:\n`diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py:188` monkeypatches\n`_open_peer_confirmation_store` on it, and `diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py:643` captures\nlogs on `apply_records.logger.name`. Keeping B in place preserves both unedited.\n\nThe two cluster-A helpers that call `_ensure_inbound_assignee_identity` (`:214`, `:388`) import it\nfunction-locally from `apply_inbound_records` — this module's existing idiom, preserving today's\ncall-time binding so an existing monkeypatch of that name still takes effect. That keeps the import\ngraph acyclic: `apply_inbound_records` imports `apply_inbound_events` at module level for one\ndocumented back-compat re-export (`_inbound_update_write_edit_event`, driven as\n`air._inbound_update_write_edit_event` by `test_inbound_update_assignee_mint_5200.py:241,285`); the\nevents module never imports the records module at module level.\n\nWhy this approach: it follows existing call-graph clusters rather than a line count, leaves both\nhalves in the 200-500 LOC band with 350+ lines of headroom each, and changes no behavioural\nassertion.\n\n## Scope\n- `.../rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py` — NEW; receives cluster A verbatim.\n- `.../rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py` — keeps cluster B; drops the module-level imports\n  cluster A owned (keeping `_extract_name`); one documented re-export.\n- `.../rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound.py` — repoint the phase-helper imports (`:34-47`) at the new\n  module; `_inbound_update_apply_links` still comes from `apply_inbound_records`.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_inbound_apply_seam_split.py` — NEW seam regression test.\n- Path anchors keyed to the OLD location of moved lines, retargeted in this same change (each is a\n  location anchor; no assertion is weakened):\n  - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py:62` — the single-`\"jira\"`-literal census\n    is keyed to `apply_inbound_records.py`, but that literal is `validate_creation_channel(\"jira\")`\n    at `:222`, inside cluster A.\n  - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_live_oracles_discriminate_5200.py:217` — its `writers`\n    tuple is keyed on file name (its docstring: \"must be retargeted whenever one moves\"); the\n    `f\"rebar-id:{local_id}\"` literal it asserts is at `:292`, inside cluster A.\n  - `docs/code-navigation.md:61,80` + `tests/unit/test_agents_serena_untyped_receiver.py:62`.\n    Worked example: doc line 61 reads ``- `src/.../apply_inbound_records.py:231` —`` and line 80\n    ``- `apply_inbound_records.py:228```; BOTH cite `_inbound_create_writeback_jira` (cluster A) and\n    are the doc's ONLY occurrences of that file name, so an accurate retarget necessarily removes\n    the string the test asserts (`assert \"apply_inbound_records.py\" in doc`). Both doc lines are\n    retargeted to `apply_inbound_events.py` with refreshed line numbers, and that ONE assertion line\n    becomes `assert \"apply_inbound_events.py\" in doc`. The test's intent — the doc evidences all\n    three real `set_entity_property` call sites — is preserved and its `dispatch_one.py` /\n    `binding_store.py` assertions are untouched.\n  - `docs/event-schema.md:261` — cites `_inbound_create_write_create_event`; retargeted. ADRs are\n    historical records, left alone.\n  - `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py:54` — the config-ownership\n    `_OWNED_FILES` registry gains the new module so the split cannot shrink that gate's coverage.\n    `_MARKER_BUDGET` / `_TOTAL_MARKER_CAP` are untouched: the new file carries zero `# read-via:`\n    markers.\n\n\n## Testing\nNew `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_inbound_apply_seam_split.py`, written RED before the\nmove (its assertions fail against today's single file):\n- **Happy path (seam pinned):** `apply_inbound_records.py` contains no `_write_event_file(` call and\n  `apply_inbound_events.py` contains no `rebar.link(` / `rebar.unlink(` / `ensure_identity_for(`\n  call — the concern boundary cannot silently re-merge.\n- **Edge (headroom):** both modules are >= 100 and <= the near-cap band derived from the\n  single-sourced limit (`LIMIT - LIMIT // 10` = 720) via `tests/module_size_support`, so neither\n  lands back in the warning list.\n- **Import-surface preservation:** all nine phase helpers plus `_RECONCILER_MARKER_APPLIER` still\n  resolve through `rebar_reconciler.apply_inbound`.\nRegression coverage is the existing suite, run unmodified (command in the criteria below).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both halves are >= 100 and <= 720 LOC — enforced by the new seam test, and independently by\n      `test $(wc -l < src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py) -le 720`.\n- [ ] `git diff --quiet origin/main -- .github/module-size-limit.txt` exits 0 (limit untouched).\n- [ ] The new seam test fails before the move (RED) and passes after (GREEN) — both runs recorded as\n      a ticket comment.\n- [ ] No behavioural assertion is modified: `git diff --stat -- tests/` lists only the new seam test\n      plus the four anchor files named in Scope, and every changed line in `git diff -- tests/` is a\n      file path, a file-name tuple entry, or an `_OWNED_FILES` entry.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler tests/scripts -m \"not integration and not external\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] `make lint` (runs `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and\n      `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`) and `make typecheck` exit 0, the ratchet\n      reporting `new=0 increased=0`.\n- [ ] For every moved symbol, Serena `find_referencing_symbols` AND\n      `grep -rn \"<name>\" src tests scripts docs` return no site that still expects it in\n      `apply_inbound_records.py`; both searches are recorded as a ticket comment.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py","reason":"NEW: receives the inbound event-file materialisation cluster (create/update phase helpers + the loop-breaker marker)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py","reason":"Keeps the rebar-facade mutation cluster (identity mint + link graph); drops the module-level imports the moved cluster owned."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound.py","reason":"Repoint the phase-helper imports at the new module."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_inbound_apply_seam_split.py","reason":"NEW: RED-first seam regression test pinning the concern boundary and the headroom."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py","reason":"Path anchor: the single-jira-literal census is keyed to the file that now holds the create-event writer."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/